x20|n|A rope, chain, or rod attached to anything to steady it; as: a rope to steady or guide an object which is being hoisted or lowered; a rope which holds in place the end of a boom, spar, or yard in a ship; a chain or wire rope connecting a suspension bridge with the land on either side to prevent lateral swaying; a rod or rope attached to the top of a structure, as of a derrick, and extending obliquely to the ground, where it is fastened. ; A grotesque effigy, like that of Guy Fawkes, dressed up in England on the fifth of November, the day of the Gunpowder Plot. ; A person of queer looks or dress.	a:22wb,67,4;1dmd,39,3;1dky,19,4;1thb,15,4~1dky,19,4;22wb,67,4;1thb,15,4;1dmd,39,3	V:1ta7,32,4~1ta7,32,4	n:22wb,73,6~22wb,73,6
